<header class="start-masthead"><p class="eyebrow">Lab runtime · proposed documentation</p><h1>Packages, installation and rollback</h1><p>Select exact public bytes and protect host dependencies before changing an installation.</p><p class="source-note">Draft prepared on 2026-10-14. Integration and final T21 qualification remain pending.</p></header>

<section id="runtime-packages-choose-the-package-boundary" aria-labelledby="runtime-packages-choose-the-package-boundary-title"><h2 id="runtime-packages-choose-the-package-boundary-title">Choose the package boundary</h2>

<p>A source package, a public export, an installed dependency/runtime and an activated consumer are different artifacts. The <a href="research/sources/product/lab/release-candidates/v1/interface/api-integration-v16/package_export.py">captured export</a> and <a href="research/sources/product/lab/release-candidates/v1/interface/api-integration-v16/package_import.py">import</a> implementations bind selected records/files and prepare bounded plans; they do not grant access to every source file or admit imported candidates.</p>

<p>Private credentials, policy/proof bodies, Session notes and protected host dependencies are not ordinary export material. Keep selected public source bytes, manifest/digest closure, original refs and intended scope explicit.</p>

</section>

<section id="runtime-packages-check-exact-bytes-and-current-effects" aria-labelledby="runtime-packages-check-exact-bytes-and-current-effects-title"><h2 id="runtime-packages-check-exact-bytes-and-current-effects-title">Check exact bytes and current effects</h2>

<p>Before export/import, resolve the declared record revisions, source/ontology cuts, permitted targets, request/envelope keys, byte bounds and current channel. A valid package envelope without its exact payload/hash/reference closure is insufficient.</p>

<p>Materialization and installation must compare actual preimages and refuse unsafe paths, foreign files and changed selectors. Preserve the original signed/native source trail separately from generated files. A changed publisher destination or dependency family requires a reviewed successor selection; do not rename a stale manifest to make it current.</p>

</section>

<section id="runtime-packages-separate-install-from-activate" aria-labelledby="runtime-packages-separate-install-from-activate-title"><h2 id="runtime-packages-separate-install-from-activate-title">Separate install from activate</h2>

<div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Stage</th><th scope="col">Result and limit</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Dependency package selection</td><td>Exact executable/library/wheel/environment input pins</td></tr><tr><td>Installation</td><td>Files exist in the selected owned layout and match expected modes/bytes</td></tr><tr><td>Verification/replay</td><td>Selected code can check the declared public/current inputs</td></tr><tr><td>Release preparation</td><td>Candidate package and readiness obligations recorded</td></tr><tr><td>Activation/publication</td><td>Separate authority and actual operational outcome</td></tr></tbody></table></div>

<p>The <a href="research/sources/product/lab/release-candidates/v1/interface/api-integration-v16/r02_installer.py">R02 installer</a> and <a href="research/sources/product/lab/release-candidates/v1/interface/api-integration-v16/release_readiness.py">release-readiness code</a> own bounded development paths. The existing installation0004 supports this preparation&#x27;s selected environment; its prior tests do not replace a fresh setup/upgrade/rollback witness for the final runtime.</p>

</section>

<section id="runtime-packages-rollback-and-interruption" aria-labelledby="runtime-packages-rollback-and-interruption-title"><h2 id="runtime-packages-rollback-and-interruption-title">Rollback and interruption</h2>

<p>Keep the prior installation and exact rollback dependencies until the new version has its own readiness and end-to-end acceptance. Inspect uncertainty after interruption before cleanup. Remove only retained-approved owned temporary files; foreign/unknown residue is preserved.</p>

<p>For local state, cold replay verifies original commits and current source bytes. For derived files, verify their source cut, manifest, selected attachment and complete receipt rather than trusting a directory name. The <a href="research/sources/docs/plans/0011-lab-runtime-completion/runs/0001-execution/T14/mixed-target-publisher-0002/README.md">publisher successor</a> illustrates ordinary filesystem no-replace and receipt boundaries, with native mixed-target integration still separate.</p>

</section>

<section id="runtime-packages-current-blocker-and-next-review" aria-labelledby="runtime-packages-current-blocker-and-next-review-title"><h2 id="runtime-packages-current-blocker-and-next-review-title">Current blocker and next review</h2>

<p>Changed API17 remains ineligible until new family/selector/software/source/profile closure is accepted. Its old metadata cannot qualify modified code. Family4&#x27;s inherited mutable preparation inputs exposed a cycle; the <a href="research/sources/docs/plans/0011-lab-runtime-completion/runs/0001-execution/T02/family4-dependency-cycle-review-0001.json">retained diagnosis</a> requires a distinct successor, not suppressed guards.</p>

<p>A later installation tutorial must select that final version, execute setup/recovery/rollback in fresh owned paths and record original effects/cleanup. None of those actions is run by this documentation generator. Read <a href="runtime-maintenance.html">maintenance</a> for the full integration sequence.</p>

</section>

